Purpose: Make the built-in passkey authenticator (corvid/passkeys) the Linux platform authenticator: a settable hook in FidoDiscoveryFactory for the kInternal transport, registered at browser start, plus the sources and deps that compile the browser-side service into chrome/browser.
Area: passkeys
Files: device/fido/fido_discovery_factory.{h,cc} (SetLinuxPlatformDiscoveryFactory, kInternal case on Linux), chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc (RegisterLinuxPlatformDiscovery in PostBrowserStart), chrome/browser/BUILD.gn (core target: passkeys_service sources and //corvid/passkeys:browser_parts)
Rebase risk: medium because FidoDiscoveryFactory has been reshaped several times; the hook is a function pointer so //device/fido does not depend on the embedder
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)
Status: BUILT and run on 155.0.8059.39 (2026-10-18): in a real browser navigator.credentials.create() offers "This device", asks for confirmation, stores the passkey (vault and key files 0600), and navigator.credentials.get() lists it in the account picker, asks again and returns a signature; the vault reopens after a restart. Unit tests verify the ES256 signature against the attested public key. Not tested: user verification beyond the confirmation dialog, conditional UI (autofill), cross-device sync, other sites.

